<h1>Delete</h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Edit &gt; Delete</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">or by pressing</span> <b><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Del</b></span></b> <span lang="EN-GB">key.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span class="Command">Delete</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command deletes the visible selection.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Sometimes you will want to work with part of the scene. Select unnecessary data, but do not delete them if you want to use them in the future. Simply call</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span class="Command">Hide Selection</span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">command from the Edit menu (or press</span> <b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Shortcut">Shift + H</span></b><span lang="EN-GB">).</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span class="Command">Delete</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command to permanently remove selections from the document.</span></p>
